### Plain Text Version

Time Limit: 1 sec
Memory: 256 MB

Description

Edward and Alphonse are alchemists who want to perform human transmutation to revive their mother, which requires philosopher stones. Father Inc operates a factory that produces philosopher stones daily. The factory runs for n days, and on the ith day, it produces Ai stones. However, these stones have an expiry limit. Stones produced on day i can only be used for Di days. For example, if Di = 1, the stones can only be used on the day they are produced, and if Di = 2, they can be used for two days (the day they are produced and the next day).

Edward and Alphonse want to maximize their success chances in transmutation. Therefore, they seek the maximum number of stones that can be accumulated on any single day.

Input Format

* The first line of the input contains one integer T — the number of test cases.
* Then T test cases follow.
* The first line of each test case contains an integer N — the number of days.
* The second line of each test case contains N space-separated integers:
  A1, A2, ..., AN.
* The third line of each test case contains N space-separated integers:
  D1, D2, ..., DN.

Output Format

For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum number of stones that can be used on any one day.

Constraints

* 1 ≤ T ≤ 10^3
* 1 ≤ N ≤ 10^5
* 1 ≤ Ai ≤ 10^7
* 1 ≤ Di ≤ 10^7
* It is guaranteed that the sum of N over all test cases ≤ 10^7.

Sample Input 1

```text
1
5
2 3 4 1 2
2 1 1 3 2
```

Sample Output 1

```text
5
```

Sample Input 2

```text
1
5
2 3 4 1 2
2 1 3 3 2
```

Sample Output 2

```text
7
```

Note

In Sample Input 1:

* Number of stones available on day 1 = 2
* Number of stones available on day 2 = 5
* Number of stones available on day 3 = 4
* Number of stones available on day 4 = 1
* Number of stones available on day 5 = 3
* Number of stones available on day 6 = 3
* Number of stones available on day 7 = 0

Therefore, the maximum number of stones available on any day is 5, which occurs on day 2.



#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

vector<long long> ps;
vector<long long> stones;

int main()
{
    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(NULL);

    int t;
    cin >> t;

    while (t--)
    {
        int n, i;

        cin >> n;
        stones.resize(n + 1);
        ps.assign(n + 1, 0);

        for (i = 1; i <= n; i++)
            cin >> stones[i];

        for (i = 1; i <= n; i++)
        {
            long long days;
            cin >> days;
            ps[i] += stones[i];
            if (i + days <= n)
                ps[i + days] -= stones[i];
        }

        long long ans = ps[1];

        for (i = 2; i <= n; i++)
        {
            ps[i] += ps[i - 1];
            ans = max(ans, ps[i]);
        }

        cout << ans << "\n";
    }

    return 0;
}
